1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,728
Keeping up with AI news, papers and tools is hard,

2
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:07,211
and most feeds quietly narrow to what you clicked last week.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:12,970
Forager is a daily brief that stays broad, shows its sources, and asks before it learns.

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,395
Setup starts with one sentence about me.

5
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:23,881
Instead of asking me to write more, Forager splits it into directions

6
00:00:23,967 --> 00:00:26,903
and asks about each with options I can just click.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,121
It suggests nearby fields too, like AI copyright policy,

8
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:34,321
and offers to follow Sora 2 for two weeks only.

9
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:38,881
Nothing I don't pick goes into my profile,

10
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:41,555
and tracking stays off until I turn it on.

11
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:44,208
Each morning I get a two-layer brief.

12
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,621
Every point cites the items behind it:

13
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:51,262
click one, and I land on the item, with a summary and a link to the source.

14
00:00:51,367 --> 00:00:53,305
And each item says why it is here:

15
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:58,740
a match to one of my interests, or breadth, something next to them that I didn't ask for.

16
00:01:01,267 --> 00:01:05,369
From my ratings, Forager may propose a change to my profile,

17
00:01:05,467 --> 00:01:09,525
but it can't write anything itself: the tool pauses until I decide.

18
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:15,042
Here the evidence is camera control, a video survey and a video model, not Sora 2,

19
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:17,948
so I reject it and approve video generation.

20
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:26,116
Breadth stays visible: no topic may take more than forty percent,

21
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,324
and I set the exploration share.

22
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:32,289
Code checks every digest, and then a separate Critic checks meaning.

23
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:37,327
Here it caught a claim the source never made, and the point was rewritten.

24
00:01:39,967 --> 00:01:46,410
Across thirty recorded digests, the team with rules raised breadth from 23 to about 37 percent,

25
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,146
and items worth reading held at about 88.
